    "q-171876": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171876",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider a triangle $△RST,$ where $m∠R=2x+{3}^{∘},$ $m∠S=4x$ and $m∠T=x+{2}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of the measures of the interior angles must be ${180}^{∘}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x+{3}^{∘})+(4x)+(x+{2}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 7x+{5}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 7x & ={175}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={25}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
