    "q-77535": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77535",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163281/assets/0086a1608c554544cdfc3337e5df136ada8986743ebc2329f262ffc90dbe28e7.png)\n\nFind the measure of angle $A$ given that $m∠B=m∠C.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using $m∠B=m∠C,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠B & =m∠C \\\\ z+{10}^{∘} & =2z \\\\ z & ={10}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, substituting $z={10}^{∘}$ in the expression for $m∠C,$ we get\n\n$$\nm∠C=2({10}^{∘})={20}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find $m∠A$ using the fact that the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A+2m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A+2\\cdot {20}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A & ={140}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77535-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{135}^{∘}",
              "html": " <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"52\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.393em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>135</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>  "
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77535-b",
